{"id":"claim:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition--kana-writing-prior-to-batchelor","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition","topics":["topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition","topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition--hepburn-tradition"],"statement":{"en":"Prior to the introduction of Batchelor's romanization system, written Ainu in Japan was recorded, if at all, using the Japanese kana syllabary.","ja":"ジョン・バチェラーによるローマ字表記法の考案以前、日本国内においてアイヌ語は書かれるとしても日本語の仮名文字で表記されていた。"},"type":"other","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universally","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0012-04","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0013-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition--forms-in-older-records-of-the-tokachi-dialect","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition","topics":["topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition","topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition--dialect-mixture"],"statement":{"en":"Forms in older records of the Tokachi dialect transcribed as ruwe sitapan should be analyzed as ru estap an.","ja":"十勝方言の過去の記録で ruwe sitapan のようにあるものは ru estap an だと考えて良い。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/central/tokachi"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ru estap an","ruwe sitapan"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0399-02","stance":"proposes"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition--yukie-chiri-1923-in-ainu-shin-y-sh","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition","topics":["topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition","topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition--echo-vowels"],"statement":{"en":"Yukie Chiri (1923) in Ainu Shin'yōshū was the first to clearly distinguish syllable-final /-r/ from /rV/, establishing the standard orthographic practice.","ja":"知里幸恵（1923）『アイヌ神謡集』において音節末の /-r/ と /rV/ が初めて明確に区別され、以降これが標準の表記となった。"},"type":"other","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-r","kor","kar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0028-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition--whereas-chiri-yukie-s-orthography-distinguishes-syllable-final","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition","topics":["topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition","topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition--echo-vowels"],"statement":{"en":"Whereas Chiri Yukie's orthography distinguishes syllable-final -r from r followed by a vowel, Batchelor's orthography writes all instances as r followed by a vowel (e.g. nukara for nukar, pirika for pirka).","ja":"知里幸恵の表記では区別されている音節末の -r と r＋母音が、バチェラーの表記ではすべて r＋母音で表記されている。"},"type":"other","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["nukar","pirka"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0053-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition--ainu-phonemically-has-words-without-final-vowels-including","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition","topics":["topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition","topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition--echo-vowels"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu phonemically has words without final vowels (including after /-r-/), although Batchelor often erroneously recorded final vowels on them.","ja":"音素的には（/-r-/の後を含め）語末母音を持たない語において、バチェラーはしばしば誤って語末母音を記録している。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-r-"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0050-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition--batchelor-s-dictionary-and-the-grammar-preceding-it","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition","topics":["topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition","topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition--reading-today"],"statement":{"en":"Batchelor's dictionary and the grammar preceding it are extremely inaccurate and cannot be relied upon as primary sources for the study of Ainu, though they contain usable material when approached critically.","ja":"バチェラーの辞書およびそれに先行する文法論は極めて不正確でありアイヌ語研究の第一資料としては信頼できないが、批判的に扱えば有用な資料も含んでいる。"},"type":"other","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0012-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition--in-a-number-of-instances-in-batchelor-s","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition","topics":["topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition","topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition--reading-today"],"statement":{"en":"In a number of instances in Batchelor's dictionary, the English glosses are much closer to the actual meaning than the Japanese translations, which are totally misleading.","ja":"バチェラーの辞書では、日本語の訳が完全に誤解を招くものである一方で、英語の訳のほうがはるかに的を射ている例が散見される。"},"type":"other","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0013-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition--in-batchelor-s-romanization-system-ainu-ci-t","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition","topics":["topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition","topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition--segments"],"statement":{"en":"In Batchelor's romanization system, Ainu ci [tʃi] is written as chi, and palatalized s is written as sh.","ja":"バチェラーのローマ字表記法では、アイヌ語の ci [tʃi] を chi で表し、口蓋化した s を sh で表す。"},"type":"other","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ci","chi","sh"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kirikae1997@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0010-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition--batchelor-kindaichi-and-chiri-yukie-all-made-use","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition","topics":["topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition","topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition--segments"],"statement":{"en":"Batchelor, Kindaichi, and Chiri Yukie all made use of voiced stop letters b, d, and g in addition to voiceless p, t, and k in their romanized orthographies.","ja":"バチェラー、金田一京助、知里幸恵の表記はいずれも、無声音 p, t, k のほかに有声音 b, d, g も用いて表記している。"},"type":"other","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["b","d","g","p","t","k","neanpe","inkar=as"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0053-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition--in-chiri-1942-syllable-initial-h-and-syllable","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition","topics":["topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition","topic:sources/historical-orthographies-and-the-batchelor-tradition--segments"],"statement":{"en":"In Chiri (1942), syllable-initial h and syllable-final x were analyzed as two distinct consonant phonemes within a twelve-consonant inventory.","ja":"知里（1942）では、hとxは12ある音韻として存在する子音の中で互いに別の音素として位置づけられていた。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["h","x"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0054-01","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
